==Jia Zhang - Research
~~~
== Research Interests
- AI for Education

- Computer Networks

- Transport Protocols and Low-Latency Services

- Routing Security\n

== Selected Research
My work focuses on secure, intelligent, and low-latency networked systems. Below are three representative research directions led as first or corresponding author.

~~~
{}{raw}
<div class="research-highlights">
  <div class="research-card" data-project="01">
    <div class="research-figure">
      <img src="photos/research/hecate-overview.png" alt="Hecate multi-source route origin validation architecture" />
      <div class="research-figure-caption">Hecate: Multi-Source Route Origin Validation</div>
    </div>
    <div class="research-copy">
      <div class="research-kicker">Routing Security</div>
      <h3>Reliable Route Origin Validation with Multi-Source Data</h3>
      <p>Hecate combines RPKI ROAs, IRR records, global BGP observations, and local routing data to improve the coverage, timeliness, and accuracy of route origin validation. Complementing this systems work, Right the Ship studies why many ROV-invalid routes are nevertheless legitimate and offers practical guidance for safer filtering.</p>
      <p class="research-work"><span class="role-badge">First author</span><span class="research-venue">TIFS '26</span> <em>From Unknown to Known</em> <span class="status-inline">Accepted</span><br /><span class="role-badge">Corresponding author</span><span class="research-venue">CCS '25</span> <em>Right the Ship</em></p>
      <div class="research-actions"><a class="research-live-link" href="http://rpki.qcl.edu.cn/#/cro" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hecate Live System</a><a href="right_the_ship-ccs25.pdf">CCS paper PDF</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="research-card research-card-wide" data-project="02">
    <div class="research-figure">
      <img src="photos/research/qudit-attack-flow.png" alt="QUDIT receiver-driven attack flow against delay-based QUIC congestion control" />
      <div class="research-figure-caption">QUDIT: Receiver-Driven Attack Workflow</div>
    </div>
    <div class="research-copy">
      <div class="research-kicker">Transport Security</div>
      <h3>Receiver-Driven Attacks on QUIC Congestion Control</h3>
      <p>QUDIT exposes a protocol-level vulnerability in which a malicious QUIC receiver manipulates Host Delay feedback to distort the RTT estimates used by delay-based congestion-control algorithms. The attack requires only ordinary receiver access, without bottleneck visibility or packet injection.</p>
      <p class="research-outcome"><strong>Key result.</strong> QUDIT reduces victim throughput by up to 60% within 0.3 seconds, with amplification gains of 200&times; to 600&times;.</p>
      <p class="research-work"><span class="role-badge">Corresponding author</span><span class="research-venue">ICNP '25</span> <em>Undermining Delay-based QUIC Congestion Control</em></p>
      <div class="research-actions"><a href="qudit-icnp25.pdf">Paper PDF</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="research-card" data-project="03">
    <div class="research-figure">
      <img src="photos/research/wisetrans-overview.png" alt="WiseTrans architecture for adaptive transport protocol selection" />
      <div class="research-figure-caption">WiseTrans: Adaptive Transport Protocol Selection</div>
    </div>
    <div class="research-copy">
      <div class="research-kicker">AI-Driven Networking</div>
      <h3>Intelligent Transport for Mobile Web Services</h3>
      <p>Across WiseTrans, Floo, and WiseStart, I developed learning-assisted mechanisms that select transport protocols, switch congestion-control algorithms using application-level QoE, and accelerate connection startup with prior knowledge. These systems were implemented and evaluated in large-scale mobile web services.</p>
      <p class="research-outcome"><strong>Key results.</strong> The systems reduce request completion time by up to 25.8%, improve QoE by 14.3% on average, and reduce first above-the-fold time by 25.43%.</p>
      <p class="research-work"><span class="role-badge">First author</span><span class="research-venue">WWW '24</span> WiseStart &nbsp; <span class="research-venue">ATC '23</span> Floo &nbsp; <span class="research-venue">ToN '23</span> WiseTrans</p>
      <div class="research-actions"><a href="wisestart_www24.pdf">WiseStart PDF</a><a href="Floo_atc23.pdf">Floo PDF</a><a href="wisetrans-ton23.pdf">WiseTrans PDF</a></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
